# Generated outputs ARE committed, so a reader can inspect the manuscript,
# figures, exports and audits without installing anything or running the
# pipeline. They remain fully regenerable — `scripts/run_kernels.py` and the
# render pipeline rebuild them from source, and the freshness validator fails if
# a committed artifact drifts from what the current source produces.
#
# The surrounding monorepo ignores output/ globally, so un-exclude it here first;
# a repository-level .gitignore outranks core.excludesFile.
!output/
!output/**
#
# What stays out is build detritus with no reader value: LaTeX intermediates and
# renderer logs, which change on every run and would churn the history.
output/**/*.aux
output/**/*.bbl
output/**/*.blg
output/**/*.fdb_latexmk
output/**/*.fls
output/**/*.log
output/**/*.nav
output/**/*.out
output/**/*.snm
output/**/*.toc
.coverage
.coverage.*
# Coverage JSON export drifts the instant src/ changes (a committed copy reported
# 98.85% while measuring only 16 of 78 tracked files). Regenerate on demand via
# `uv run pytest --cov=src --cov-report=json:coverage_project.json`; never commit it.
coverage_project.json
.pytest_cache/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
.benchmarks/
tmp/
.playwright-cli/

# Egg-info from local installs (any location — guards against renamed-fork drift).
**/*.egg-info/

# Project-local virtualenvs (root .venv is shared)
.venv/

# Local SkillTree bootstrap credentials and trusted-client secrets.
.active_skillference_local/
